A good weapon for a neutral character.  One task might be
to work at altars until you have a good enough one-handed
weapon.  It sucks to have a cursed two-handed weapon even
as nice as Cleaver.

> a pair of gloves, Dwarvish mithril,

Here's another thing you need to be doing at this point.
Gather better armor.  You should try on any armor you know
isn't cursed and swap for the lowest AC possible.  But you
also want to pick specific types in favor of AC at times.
A simple case is that dwarvish mithril - either type of mithril
is so much lighter than the 3 types of plate the plate isn't
worth switching to.

If you can find speed, jump, kick, water walking boots, they
go in place of mundane ones.  And if you get to pick among
tham probably that's the order.  Dexterity or power gloves
same comment.  Brilliance, esp helmets same comment.
Cloaks are very much a matter of taste as to which is the
good one but orcish/dwarvish cloak isn't the best type.  And
the best type of body armor is yet to come.

